  },
  "en": {
    "text": {
      "en": "Termius autocompleted a cd into rm -rf, but the deleted files were still held open by a running process. As long as that process lives, lsof lists the files marked (deleted) with their process IDs, and in /proc/<pid>/fd each one can be copied back to where it was by its file descriptor. For whole folders the author wrote a small Rust program that turns lsof's output into a recovery script. Over 95% of the data came back, but nothing is guaranteed: keep backups."
    },
